{"description":"Follow-up from CTX-0292 (PR #487, issue #486). The accepted CTX-0118 decoration contract now lands as config + validation + Core px solver + runtime carry/safe-mode. Missing: live present-path painting.

Deliverable: consume Runtime::decorated_allocations() (or equivalent px frames) in the present path so gaps_out/gaps_in bands, border rings, and radius clipping are actually rendered. This requires:
1. Fractional-cell View frame composition: per-view grid/frame derivation from px frames (today the container is one global cell grid and leaves are cell rects);
2. A renderer radius primitive (FillRect has no radius/border) plus software/GPU parity and HiDPI scaling — CTX-0238g stage-2 render-owner lane owns the radius mechanism; coordinate/merge order with that task;
3. Hit-testing and input mapping updated to the decorated frames (frame for hit testing, content for painting), preserving CTX-0177 cell-gap behavior.
Acceptance: headless RGBA/frame evidence for gaps/border/radius, safe-mode 0/0/1/0 rendering, no regressions in the existing panel-gap visual tests.

Priority: P2 | Area: render | Labels: feat,area:render,P2 | Milestone: v0.1.0 | RFC: CTX-0118 | Task: CTX-0292 (follow-up)","displayId":"CTX-0294","id":"01M25HXQBVVMP0ZWB1A7DQVATF","priority":"normal","status":"ready","title":"Wire Core-owned px decoration into live present (gaps_out/gaps_in/border/radius painting)"}

{"description":"Follow-up from CTX-0294 (PR wiring minimal rounded border ring via FillRect scanline geometry). The minimal ring paints the outer frame silhouette, gap bands, and straight border edges on both backends by construction, but does NOT clip glyph/cell sub-cell overhang at the four inner corner arcs, and emits per-corner-row fills instead of a fragment SDF.

Deliverable: DrawList radius/border primitive with hyprland-style SDF (or mask) support in the wgpu present shader plus software parity, inner-arc content clipping (scissor/mask so text never overdraws the curve), HiDPI physical-px semantics, and headless RGBA goldens; retire the CTX-0294 scanline ring if the primitive supersedes it.

Priority: P2 | Area: render | Labels: feat,area:render,P2 | Milestone: v0.1.0 | RFC: CTX-0118 | Task: CTX-0294 (follow-up, CTX-0238g stage 2)","displayId":"CTX-0311","id":"01M265DK4MT0Q1EGH1Q7Y8W0P1","priority":"normal","status":"ready","title":"Renderer stage-2 radius primitive: SDF rounded fills + inner-arc glyph clipping (CTX-0238g)"}

{"description":"Follow-up finding from CTX-0294 live wiring. State::resize reflows width and height in one pass; blank rows below the content are collected as physical rows, so shrinking height by one in the same call as a width change moves the top content row into scrollback while the grid keeps the blank tail (observed: 80x24 "hello world" -> resize(38,23) yields sb=1 and a blank grid). The runtime works around it with a two-phase resize (width at old height, then height-only) in Runtime::resize_primary_grid and pane sync, but the underlying State::resize semantics remain surprising and are untested for this shape.

Deliverable: decide and test the intended one-call semantic (keep cursor-anchored bottom-align for real content but not drop top content behind trailing blanks), and remove the runtime workaround once State::resize preserves the visible content.

Priority: P2 | Area: term-state | Labels: fix,area:term-state,P2 | Milestone: v0.1.0 | Task: CTX-0294 (follow-up)","displayId":"CTX-0312","id":"01M265DMBVPF231TRM0WPXJ9SD","priority":"normal","status":"ready","title":"term-state: one-call width+height shrink bottom-aligns top content into scrollback"}

