{"content":"Implemented cell-box block rasterization (U+2580-U+259F) in bitty-render. Root cause: at 1.6x (19.2pt, 16x35 cell) the font U+2588 bitmap's rightmost coverage column averages 88/255 and baseline placement starts one pixel above the cell; adjacent cells therefore expose a partial font edge instead of a full cell edge. Fix: new crate-private block rasterizer emits exact-cell masks (eighth-boundary rects; uniform 25/50/75% shade coverage) and places them through a reserved atlas namespace on the normal glyph layer; shaped path delegates single block scalars to the same emitter. Box drawing, braille, CJK, and Terminal Truth stay on the existing paths.

Tests: cargo nextest -p bitty-render -p bitty-terminal = 1616 passed, 1 skipped. fmt clean; clippy -p bitty-render -p bitty-terminal --all-targets -D warnings clean. New headless tests cover 1.6x horizontal and vertical U+2588 adjacency (every boundary pixel 255), shades 25/50/75%, all 32 block scalars, box/braille non-interception, and a golden hash (old 0b6845d31fa25c75 -> new d86f265d11fc1845).

Live repro on Hyprland workspace 5 (scale 1.6): recording/ctx-2307-block-seams/before-bitty-main.png, after-bitty-ctx-1387.png, kitty-same-font.png, compare-after-kitty.png, compare-0023-kitty-provided.png. Before/after release hashes: before sha256 5e124be4..., after sha256 03405e4a.... Desktop restored; no processes left running.","display_id":"PX-7543","id":"01M5BY6ZFQP63S7QJ5A5WR9HDV","item_type":"note","status":"open","task_id":"01M5BW7NKJJCHJBTFN1KCVY9DF"}

