{"description":"Priority: P0 | Area: platform | Labels: fix,P0,area:platform,area:stability | Milestone: v0.0.29 | RFC: OQ-2570 | Task: assign display id

Follow-up to bitty#2570 and the merged synthetic visibility/retry fixes in #2588, #2662, and #2668.

## Scope

Determine and, if needed, fix the platform event path for real compositor workspace hide/show transitions:

- verify which winit/platform events are delivered for Hyprland workspace unmap/remap;
- verify whether `Suspended`/`Resumed` reaches `Runtime::set_surface_visibility_at` for the real event path;
- preserve the current hidden presentation gate, retained damage, deferred reveal, bounded retry, and Terminal Truth semantics;
- do not re-enable `WindowEvent::Occluded(true)` blindly or introduce a weaker fallback transport;
- add deterministic event-plumbing tests for every accepted event mapping and fail-closed behavior;
- prepare an owner-authorized, isolated Hyprland campaign plan/evidence schema for 100+ workspace switch cycles, without touching the owner's desktop in automated work.

## Non-goals

No release/tag/CDN/R2 changes, no render-thread redesign, no signal-handler implementation, no live campaign without explicit owner authorization, and no claim that the original compositor root cause is fixed until representative evidence exists.

## Acceptance

- The real event mapping and its limitations are documented with source/test evidence.
- Any code change is minimal, scoped to platform visibility plumbing, and mutation-sensitive.
- Headless/runtime tests prove no hidden presentation attempt and deferred reveal behavior.
- Live Hyprland evidence remains a separate owner-authorized gate.","displayId":"CTX-1539","id":"01M5RVS7HTFD7YZY964WGHE73C","priority":"urgent","status":"ready","title":"[0.0.29] Prove workspace occlusion visibility event plumbing"}

