{"description":"Priority: P1 | Area: pty | Labels: fix,area:pty,P1 | Milestone: v0.0.29 | RFC: CTX-1020/CTX-1029 | Task: CTX-1561

Harden the FreeBSD PTY size assertion against the known emulated-VM spawn race that failed the v0.0.29 release FreeBSD job.

Scope:
- `crates/bitty-pty/tests/spawn_smoke.rs::cat_echo_resize_and_graceful_shutdown` read `(0, 0)` from `Pty::size()` immediately after spawn on FreeBSD 15.1 (vmactions VM, `--test-threads=4`), while the sibling pixel-geometry test passed in the same binary and the same commit passed the nightly BSD tier;
- confirm the mechanism (child lost to the documented FreeBSD parallel-spawn TIOCSCTTY/SIGHUP race versus a genuine winsize wiring gap) before changing behavior;
- fix without masking a real "initial size never applied" regression: bounded liveness check and/or bounded settle re-query, one bounded respawn at most, named constants documenting the race;
- keep Linux/macOS behavior unchanged; scope limited to the bitty-pty crate;
- verify with `cargo test -p bitty-pty --locked`, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `cargo clippy -p bitty-pty --all-targets` under a task-scoped target dir that is removed afterwards.","displayId":"CTX-1561","id":"01M5SZWE0T7X7FZXACTV58NGN0","priority":"high","status":"ready","title":"[0.0.29] Harden FreeBSD PTY size assertion"}

