Mod+n Spiral placement only rotates the insertion side; the split axis still comes from the cell-aspect heuristic, so the clockwise Right-Down-Left-Up rotation collapses to Right-Right-Left-Left on normal windows. Derive the axis from the spiral phase (Right/Left horizontal, Down/Up vertical), degrade to the perpendicular axis when the phase axis cannot host two gap-aware 10x4 panes, and keep the largest-feasible Balanced fallback with spiral_phase=None when neither fits. Add headless tests pinning the axis sequence and the degradation.","priority":"high","required_role":"backend","title":"[0.0.30] Fix Spiral axis rotation for Mod+n panel placement"},"before":{"description":"Priority: P1 | Area: ui | Labels: fix,P1,area:ui | Milestone: v0.0.30 | RFC: OQ-SPIRAL | Task: assign display id

